cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use OACT in your work, please cite it using these metadata."
title: >-
  Open Analytics Control Tower (OACT): A Public-Interest Infrastructure
  Resilience System
abstract: >-
  OACT is an open-source, reproducible decision-support system that turns public
  extreme-weather and infrastructure signals into explainable, county-level
  supply-chain disruption risk assessments. It models compound risk — storm
  sequencing, antecedent soil saturation and hydrologic stress — and translates
  model output into auditable Go / Monitor / No-Go decision support. The
  reference implementation scores county-level power disruption risk in
  California and replays the January 2023 atmospheric-river event cluster.
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Resilient-Supply-Chain/open-supply-chain-control-tower"
